#Rigid-group definitions for RNA, springs-only articulated model: the whole
#backbone (alpha..zeta), the glycosidic chi, the 2'-OH rotor, and the sugar
#pucker, all as free hinges in an otherwise rigid mesh. No bonded energy of
#any kind -- every spring here carries pdb2spn's uniform --stiffness.
#Companion file for DNA: DNAAtomRigidGroups.rbody, whose header carries the
#full derivation of the group/hinge layout. Only what differs for RNA is
#repeated here.
#
#SINGLE STRAND. Nothing in this file couples two chains -- the format has no
#notion of chain, +/- only walk the sequence. That is the natural fit for RNA,
#which is normally one strand; its own secondary structure (hairpins, stems)
#is base pairing, so it must come from the hydrogen-bond mechanism
#(biospring's hbond.* settings and a .hbond donor/acceptor table), never from
#a rigid-body rule. A stem-loop built with this file and no hbond term will
#simply unfold into an open strand.
#
#TWO DIFFERENCES FROM DNA, both on C2':
#  - the 2'-OH replaces one of the two 2' hydrogens, so _C2 lists O2' where
#    the DNA file lists H2'2. Atom names follow amber99sb.xml: O2' and HO'2
#    (the hydroxyl hydrogen is HO'2, not H2'2 -- easy to misread).
#  - that hydroxyl is a real rotor, so it gets its own _O2 group overlapping
#    _C2 on exactly {C2', O2'}. This is the same construction as Ser/Thr/Tyr
#    hydroxyls in ProteinAtomRigidGroups.rbody.
#
#The 2'-OH is also why RNA sits overwhelmingly in the C3'-endo (North)
#pucker where B-DNA sits in C2'-endo: the substituent disfavours the South
#basin sterically and electronically. This file does not encode that
#preference, and it does not leave the pucker free either: see the DNA
#file's header for why a five-membered ring cannot be freed by per-vertex
#groups (measured 10/10 -- fixing bonds and angles rigidifies a 5-ring).
#The sugar is therefore rigid here too, frozen at the input structure's
#pucker. Reproducing a genuine bimodal North/South distribution is the job
#of the bonded parameters, and for RNA it is the single most important
#thing to validate once they exist.

#Adenine ------------------------------------------------------------------
A_P    RA  -O3' P O1P O2P O5'
A_O5   RA  P O5' C5'
A_C5   RA  O5' C5' H5'1 H5' H5'2 H5'' C4'
A_C4   RA  C5' C4' H4' O4' C3'
A_O4   RA  C4' O4' C1'
A_C1   RA  O4' C1' H1' C2' N9
A_C2   RA  C1' C2' H2'1 H2' O2' C3'
A_O2   RA  C2' O2' HO'2 HO2'
A_C3   RA  C2' C3' H3' C4' O3'
A_O3   RA  C3' O3' +P
A_BASE RA  C1' N9 C8 H8 N7 C5 C6 N6 H61 H62 N1 C2 H2 N3 C4
A_5TER RA  H5T O5' C5'
A_3TER RA  C3' O3' H3T

#Cytosine -----------------------------------------------------------------
C_P    RC  -O3' P O1P O2P O5'
C_O5   RC  P O5' C5'
C_C5   RC  O5' C5' H5'1 H5' H5'2 H5'' C4'
C_C4   RC  C5' C4' H4' O4' C3'
C_O4   RC  C4' O4' C1'
C_C1   RC  O4' C1' H1' C2' N1
C_C2   RC  C1' C2' H2'1 H2' O2' C3'
C_O2   RC  C2' O2' HO'2 HO2'
C_C3   RC  C2' C3' H3' C4' O3'
C_O3   RC  C3' O3' +P
C_BASE RC  C1' N1 C6 H6 C5 H5 C4 N4 H41 H42 N3 C2 O2
C_5TER RC  H5T O5' C5'
C_3TER RC  C3' O3' H3T

#Guanine ------------------------------------------------------------------
G_P    RG  -O3' P O1P O2P O5'
G_O5   RG  P O5' C5'
G_C5   RG  O5' C5' H5'1 H5' H5'2 H5'' C4'
G_C4   RG  C5' C4' H4' O4' C3'
G_O4   RG  C4' O4' C1'
G_C1   RG  O4' C1' H1' C2' N9
G_C2   RG  C1' C2' H2'1 H2' O2' C3'
G_O2   RG  C2' O2' HO'2 HO2'
G_C3   RG  C2' C3' H3' C4' O3'
G_O3   RG  C3' O3' +P
G_BASE RG  C1' N9 C8 H8 N7 C5 C6 O6 N1 H1 C2 N2 H21 H22 N3 C4
G_5TER RG  H5T O5' C5'
G_3TER RG  C3' O3' H3T

#Uracil -------------------------------------------------------------------
#Uracil is thymine without the 5-methyl: it carries H5 where DT has C7 and
#its three hydrogens. Nothing else differs, so no methyl rotor is needed
#here (see the DNA file's thymine note).
U_P    RU  -O3' P O1P O2P O5'
U_O5   RU  P O5' C5'
U_C5   RU  O5' C5' H5'1 H5' H5'2 H5'' C4'
U_C4   RU  C5' C4' H4' O4' C3'
U_O4   RU  C4' O4' C1'
U_C1   RU  O4' C1' H1' C2' N1
U_C2   RU  C1' C2' H2'1 H2' O2' C3'
U_O2   RU  C2' O2' HO'2 HO2'
U_C3   RU  C2' C3' H3' C4' O3'
U_O3   RU  C3' O3' +P
U_BASE RU  C1' N1 C6 H6 C5 H5 C4 O4 N3 H3 C2 O2
U_5TER RU  H5T O5' C5'
U_3TER RU  C3' O3' H3T
